---
import { site } from '../data/site.js';
---
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="audience-title">
  <div class="wrap narrow">
    <h2 id="audience-title">A standard, not an optimization strategy</h2>
    <p>
      Bare Bones SEO is an open-source attempt to establish better conventions for managing technical SEO settings. We focus on transparency, consistency, owner control, and minimal overhead—not keywords, content scores, or ranking recommendations. Verification matters too: what a website actually publishes should match its settings.
    </p>
    <p>
      The WordPress plugin and static-site specification are practical starting points, not claims of widespread industry adoption. Both are open source: inspect the <a href={site.github}>WordPress implementation</a> and <a href={site.staticGithub}>static-site specification</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .narrow { max-width: var(--measure); margin-inline: auto; margin-left: max(1.25rem, calc((100% - var(--wide)) / 2)); }
  h2 { font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.2vw, 2.4rem); }
  p { margin-top: var(--space-2); color: var(--ink-soft); }
  h2 + p { margin-top: var(--space-3); }
</style>
